  (no_connect (at 99.06 96.52) (uuid 0b9473da-5d77-5c41-a8cf-730d3a300ce4))
  (text "R-LED-PD holds the input low through the bootloader window: GPIO1 floats, OE is tied low,\nand a floating AHCT input would put clean 5 V edges into the strip before firmware runs.\nBI is grounded at the head of the strip; from the second pixel on, BI comes from inside the tape.\nGates B-D are spare: inputs and enables tied low (an enabled CMOS gate never floats)." (at 40.64 233.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid be312523-6edd-5047-b074-eae0a15ca140))
  (text "FROM THE HAND-WRITTEN NETLIST THIS SHEET REPLACES (verbatim; the part notes are on each part's Note field):\n\nAUTHORITATIVE for connectivity. The ASCII drawing in led-strip-drive.md is a REPRESENTATION of this file. THE\nSTRIP IS NOT IN THIS FILE and cannot be: it is a length of tape on the far side of a connector, addressable\nLEDs with their own supply. J-LED is the boundary, and the nets stop at its pins. ONE strip since ADR 0016.\n\nTHE FOUR ENABLES ARE TIED LOW, which is why the pull-downs are needed rather than optional - the buffer is\nlive through the whole bootloader window. The three spare gates' inputs are tied for the reason the module's\nspare is: an enabled CMOS gate with a floating input is the one wrong answer, and the part's own row says to\ntie every unused input. BI IS A GROUND CONNECTION, NOT A DRIVEN ONE. The datasheet's recommended circuit ties\nthe first pixel's BI to its GND; from the second pixel on, BI comes from the previous pixel's DI inside the\ntape. The head has nothing to lag, so there is nothing to drive.\n\nThe three spare gates drive nothing, which is fine." (at 256.54 38.099999999999994 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 0274f84e-aa8d-5430-8e47-f906fb6a8b4c))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
